  partName: Blade
  description: The Blade is a critical component of the jet engine, responsible for
    compressing air and directing it into the combustion chamber. Its unique shape
    and size allow for optimal airflow and efficiency, making it a crucial part of
    the engine's overall performance. Interestingly, the Blade is typically made
    from high-strength, lightweight materials such as titanium or nickel alloys to
    withstand the extreme stresses and temperatures encountered during operation.
